Rule 4 (seed tensor must be a 1-D vector of length 2)
{v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) = 2
>>
Rule 5 (seed tensor dtype must be int32 or int64)
{v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 4
>>
Rule 6 (seed as a tuple of ints must have length 2)
{v_2 : tuple(int)} |= v_2.len = 2
>>
Rule 7 (seed as a list of ints must have length 2)
{v_2 : list(int)} |= v_2.len = 2
>>
Rule 8 (image must be 3-D or 4-D)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = 3 ∨ ndim(v_1) = 4)
>>
Rule 9 (spatial and channel dims must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = 3 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 2) > 0) ∨ (ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 2) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 3) > 0)
>>
Rule 10 (seed tensor must be a length-2 vector with int32 or int64 dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = 2 ∧ (dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4))
>>
Rule 11 (seed provided as a tuple must have exactly two integers)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 2
>>
Rule 12 (seed provided as a list must have exactly two integers)
{v_1 : list(int)} |= v_1.len = 2
>>
Rule 13 (seed arity when provided as list or tuple)
{v_1 : list(int) ⊎ tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 2
>>
Rule 14 (image must have either 3 or 4 dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = 3) ∨ (ndim(v_1) = 4)
